 "schema": "pcc.claim/v1",
 "scope": "Toy scale on a shared VM, each route re-run by a separate checker (A1-A3, A5, A6 fully or by subset with matching output; A4 32 of 40 closure-degree rows). 'Ruled out' is a verdict on these constructions at the measured sizes plus desk arguments that are not machine-checked, not a lower bound. Literature (McGuire-Mueller, Yokoyama et al.) known only through repo summaries; research-kb prior-art check not done. No bench.record/v1, no EKS run, no validation gate. Excludes the PKM chain with auxiliary unknowns (separate claim), Semaev m >= 5 at scale, trace bases of dimension >= 2, norm maps and GHS covers. Route table and verdicts: research/prime_field_ic_closure_20261112/closure-ledger.md section 1A and research/notes/index-calculus/PRIME_FIELD_IC_CLOSURE_20261112.md section 2.",
 "statement": "Prime-field index-calculus routes measured at toy scale and found not to beat matched Pollard rho's exponent 1/2: A1 Weil descent with the base in GF(p) lifted to GF(p^k) (no gain: the k-1 extra equations constrain only the twist component, predicted equal to measured on 12/12 targets); A2 Weil descent with a subspace base outside GF(p) (cost about p^1); A3 Galois-orbit trace base Tr(S) (coverage |Tr(S)|/#E 0.52-0.74, not shrinking with p, so |F| about 0.6p and exponent 1; measured for lines through the origin, k <= 3, m = 2, p <= 809); A5 fixed-degree polynomial-root base (exponent 1, resting mainly on the K1 counting bound |B| <= 2 deg f); A6 Semaev m = 3/4 with an interval or low-bit base (fitted cost exponents 0.69 and 0.80 for the MITM oracle, at least 1.10 for Boolean Macaulay, over 10-20 bits); A4 rational-map image bases x = phi(t) in the presentations tested (identity, t^2, t^3, Moebius, Lattes, Velu, mu_n): a relabel or a yield loss (Lattes/Velu keep 0.34-0.66 of the yield)."
}
